            "title": "Federal Signal (FSS): Five-Year Earnings Growth Deceleration Raises Valuation Debate",
            "description": "",
            "summary": "Federal Signal (FSS) posted another year of high-quality numbers, with earnings growing at an average annual rate of 21.2% over the past five years. However, that pace cooled to 9.6% in the most recent year. The company\u2019s net profit margin held steady at 11.2%, while the outlook calls for earnings growth of 11.85% and revenue growth of 10.8% per year. Both figures slightly outpace the broader US market on revenue but trail on earnings. Trading below fair value but commanding a premium...",
